{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Child-roster re-scope (executing plan-review advisories #1–#3; operator-approved 2026-08-29)\n\nThe plan-review PASS surfaced (advisory) that the epic's existing children all target **`.retired` tombstone GC**, which the proof shows shrinks the *blobless* CI-guarded pack by **~0** (`.retired` files are blobs; the guarded pack has zero blobs). The pack-shrink lever is **below-horizon commit/tree collapse**, owned by no child. Re-scoping so the epic owns the REAL levers. Nothing is dropped silently — disposition per child below.\n\n**KEEP + BROADEN (horizon/safety infra — lever-agnostic, needed by ANY reclamation):**\n- **866f `unlikely-zealous-skua` (ADR, S0):** broadened from \"retired-event GC\" to **remote-anchored below-horizon *history* reclamation** whose PRIMARY lever is commit/tree collapse (retired-event GC is a secondary companion). Still defines the N-day horizon, remote-reachability, stale-clone forced override, and the I1–I9 proof — now also the C1–C5 boundary at the commit/tree-rewrite level and the SNAPSHOT authorship-ledger carriage.\n- **e32d `able-tidy-massasauga` (horizon eligibility computation):** broadened — the \"compaction commit reachable from the sync remote's `tickets` ref ≥ N days\" check is the eligibility primitive for **collapse checkpoints**, not only `.retired` tombstones. Read-only; no deletion.\n- **aff9 `sarcastic-specified-kodiakbear` (stale-clone forced override):** **retained unchanged** — it is lever-agnostic (it enforces the C3 remote-override that makes ANY below-horizon reclamation safe against stale clones). Directly needed by the collapse rewrite.\n\n**NARROW (wrong lever for the pack, kept as secondary cleanup):**\n- **51a7 `mystical-capsizable-ibis` (branch-wide `.retired` sweep):** narrowed to a **secondary, non-pack-shrinking** cleanup — reclaims `.retired` sidecar *blobs* from full-history/working-tree packs; **~0 effect on the blobless CI-guarded pack**. Explicitly NOT the health-lane lever. Reordered to depend on the collapse mechanism (runs after, on the collapsed baseline).\n\n**NEW children owning the real levers (created under this epic):**\n- **S1 — below-horizon commit/tree collapse rewrite engine** (shadow-clone `git fast-import` collapse of derived enrichment-quartet/superseded-digest/redundant-merge commits+trees to SNAPSHOT checkpoints; ledger `position→commit_sha` re-resolution + `enforce_since` re-anchor). THE pack-shrink lever.\n- **S2 — per-backend publish-swap + rollback re-convergence** (git-ref `--force-with-lease` CAS; S3 exclusive push-locked bundle-set replacement bypassing the auto-doctor; and the advisory #4 rollback re-convergence design for clients that already reconciled onto the rewritten baseline).\n- **S3 — dry-run reclaim harness** on a throwaway shadow clone proving `rebar verify-authorship` stays clean and the pack shrinks as predicted. HARD STOP: no prod swap without a separate human go/no-go.\n- **W1 — batch enrichment+digest into one write lane** (collapses ~14K commits/day at the source; structural, durable).\n- **W2 — shard the 6,008 flat ticket dirs** in the root tree (cuts the 270 KB per-commit root-tree churn; structural, durable).\n\nPack-shrink quantification vs the 100 MiB budget (advisory #2/#3) is owned by this epic's proof (comments above) and re-asserted in the S3 dry-run's measured result. The W3 budget bridge (child `green-clerkish-noolbenger`, Gerrit 2392) is the interim health-lane fix while S1–S3 + W1/W2 land."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788046398458806295,"uuid":"53cf7928-66f5-469e-b333-4397d5959914"}